// Pre-coloring Belady/MIN register-pressure spill pass.
//
// Theory of operation: strict-SSA interference graphs are chordal, hence
// perfect, so their chromatic number equals their clique number (= MaxLive,
// the peak number of simultaneously-live values per register class). If we
// reduce MaxLive to <= k (the pool size) at every program point BEFORE
// coloring, the chordal graph is provably k-colorable and SSAColoring's
// first-fit pass cannot fail — the expensive eviction/last-chance recolor
// never fires. This is the standard Hack/Braun "spill before color" approach
// (Register Spilling and Live-Range Splitting for SSA-Form Programs, 2009).
//
// The pass observes the flat `ranges` array (virtual ranges PLUS the fixed
// pseudo-ranges minted by insertPhysicalConstraints — clobbers/params/phys-
// dest, which consume real registers at call sites) and, at every over-
// pressured point, spills the live values whose NEXT USE is farthest away
// (Belady's MIN). It produces a SpillDecision and routes it through the
// existing allocateSpillSlots -> insertSpillCode path — it emits no spill
// code itself and never mutates ranges/liveness/IR directly. The driver loop
// lives in FunctionRegAllocator.runBeladyPressureReduction; this file holds
// the analysis (pressure, next-use) and the spill picker.
//
// Why this must run AFTER insertPhysicalConstraints (so clobber pseudo-ranges
// are visible as pressure) and BEFORE colorSSA/destroySSA (destroySSA lowers
// phi to copies and destroys chordality).

// Safety belt on the number of spill-and-rebuild rounds. The infinite-weight
// invariant on reload vregs already bounds rounds (each round makes >=1 more
// vreg unspillable); this cap matches the reactive loop's iteration cap.
export let BELADY_MAX_ROUNDS = 10

// Cross-block next-use ordering unit. A value still live out of the current
// block sorts as farther than any in-block use; the next-use-block's RPO
// index is multiplied by this so cross-block ordering dominates intra-block
// tie-breaking. 1048576 (2^20, ~1M) is large enough that no realistic block has
// that many positions, yet small enough that rpoIndex * UNIT never overflows
// i64 for any realistic function. (Written as a literal, not `1 shl 20`: the
// self-hosted parser does not accept a binary operator in a module-level `let`
// initializer, only in expression contexts — and this file must self-compile.)
let BLOCK_DISTANCE_UNIT = 1048576

// Next-use distance for a value with no use at or beyond the current point
// (dead here) — spill it first, it is needed never.
let NEXT_USE_INFINITE = i64.max

// Peak register-pressure demand per register class, measured the way the
// colorer actually allocates: caller-saved and callee-saved registers are
// DISJOINT sub-pools, so a single "MaxLive vs k" total over-states pressure
// at call sites (where the 1-position caller-saved clobber pseudo-ranges pile
// up) and, worse, hides genuine callee-saved over-subscription (a crowd of
// call-crossing values is callee-saved-ONLY at EVERY point it is live).
//
// Two demands are tracked per class:
//   * `gpr`/`fp` — TOTAL distinct-register demand: live virtuals (each needs
//     one register) plus the count of DISTINCT physical registers the live
//     fixed pseudo-ranges occupy. Counting distinct registers (not raw range
//     count) is what removes the over-count: at a call the arg-setup phys-dest
//     range for x0 and the call's clobber range for x0 both pin x0 but consume
//     ONE register, so they count once. Must be <= poolSize for the chordal
//     graph to be colorable at all.
//   * `gprCallee`/`fpCallee` — CALLEE-SAVED demand: live call-crossing virtuals
//     (which the colorer can place ONLY in callee-saved registers — a caller-
//     saved one is clobbered by the intervening call) plus distinct callee-
//     saved registers pinned by fixed ranges. Must be <= the callee-saved
//     sub-pool size, independently of the total. This is the constraint that
//     was previously invisible: a function can sit at total <= k yet have far
//     more call-crossing values than callee-saved registers, which the first-
//     fit colorer cannot satisfy and the last-chance recolor then explodes on.
//
// gpr and fp are independent pools so we track them separately.
export type MaxLiveResult
	export var gpr as RegInt
	export var fp as RegInt
	export var gprCallee as RegInt
	export var fpCallee as RegInt

	export static function create(gpr RegInt, fp RegInt, gprCallee RegInt, fpCallee RegInt) returns MaxLiveResult
		return Self{gpr: gpr, fp: fp, gprCallee: gprCallee, fpCallee: fpCallee}
	end 'create'
end 'MaxLiveResult'

// True iff `ord` is a callee-saved register of `regClass` under `desc`. A
// register is callee-saved iff it is in the class pool but NOT in the class's
// caller-saved list. Linear scans over the (tiny) caller-saved list; called
// only while sizing the per-class callee-saved bitmap, not per position.
function ordinalIsCalleeSaved(ord RegOrdinal, regClass RegClass, desc TargetRegAlloc) returns bool
	let callerSaved = match regClass 'pick'
		gpr gives desc.callerSavedGprs
		fp gives desc.callerSavedFps
	end 'pick'
	for cs in callerSaved 'each'
		if cs == ord 'isCaller'
			return false
		end 'isCaller'
	end 'each'
	return true
end 'ordinalIsCalleeSaved'

// Callee-saved sub-pool size for a class: poolSize minus the caller-saved
// count. Matches the colorer's partition (crossesCall ⇒ callee-saved only).
export function calleeSavedSizeFor(regClass RegClass, desc TargetRegAlloc) returns RegInt
	return match regClass 'pick'
		gpr gives desc.gprPoolSize - desc.callerSavedGprs.count()
		fp gives desc.fpPoolSize - desc.callerSavedFps.count()
	end 'pick'
end 'calleeSavedSizeFor'

// Pool size for a class.
export function poolSizeFor(regClass RegClass, desc TargetRegAlloc) returns RegInt
	return match regClass 'pick'
		gpr gives desc.gprPoolSize
		fp gives desc.fpPoolSize
	end 'pick'
end 'poolSizeFor'

// Max physical register ordinal of a class's pool, used to size the per-
// position distinct-register occupancy bitmaps. Scans the (small) pool once.
function maxPoolOrdinalFor(regClass RegClass, desc TargetRegAlloc) returns RegInt
	let pool = match regClass 'pick'
		gpr gives desc.gprPool
		fp gives desc.fpPool
	end 'pick'
	var maxOrd = 0
	for ord in pool 'each'
		if ord > maxOrd 'higher'
			maxOrd = ord
		end 'higher'
	end 'each'
	return maxOrd
end 'maxPoolOrdinalFor'

// Per-block map blockId -> max op position in that block. Max position is
// `opRefs.count() + 1` (the terminator slot): ops 0..count-1 live at
// positions 1..count, and the terminator at count+1. Mirrors the sizing in
// buildCallPositionsPerBlock (array length = maxBlockId + 1, keyed by raw
// block.id). Blocks not in this func index a -1 sentinel.
function blockMaxPositions(module TargetModule, func IrFunction) returns RegIntArray
	var maxBlockId = 0
	for blockRef in func.blockRefs 'findMax'
		let block = try module.blocks.get(blockRef) otherwise panic("invariant: blockRef from func.blockRefs not in module.blocks")
		if block.id > maxBlockId 'higher'
			maxBlockId = block.id
		end 'higher'
	end 'findMax'

	var result = RegIntArray.create()
	var i = 0
	while i <= maxBlockId 'init'
		result.push(-1)
		i = i + 1
	end 'init'

	for blockRef in func.blockRefs 'eachBlock'
		let block = try module.blocks.get(blockRef) otherwise panic("invariant: blockRef from func.blockRefs not in module.blocks")
		try result.set(block.id, value: block.opRefs.count() + 1) otherwise panic("invariant: blockMaxPositions.set OOB; sized to maxBlockId+1")
	end 'eachBlock'

	return result
end 'blockMaxPositions'

// Per-block bucketed interval events, built in a SINGLE pass over all ranges.
//
// Both register-pressure sweeps (computeClassDemand and pickForClass) used to
// re-scan EVERY range for EVERY block to collect that block's interval events —
// an O(numBlocks × numRanges × intervals) wall on functions with thousands of
// blocks (Testing.parseSpecFile: 2223 blocks × thousands of ranges, the
// self-compile's dominant frame). Since each interval belongs to exactly one
// block, a single pass can bucket every (rangeIdx, startPos, endPos) event into
// its block's list. The per-block sweep then reads only its own bucket, making
// the total bucketing O(numRanges × intervals) once instead of per block.
//
// Parallel arrays keyed by `base[blockId] .. base[blockId+1]`: `rangeIdx[i]` is
// the range index, `startPos[i]` / `endPos[i]` its already-clamped half-open
// interval bounds in that block. Empty / out-of-bounds intervals are dropped at
// build time (they were dropped per-block before), so a consumer never re-tests
// them. `endPos` is clamped to maxPos+1 exactly as the old inline code did, so
// the event-bucket sizing (maxPos+2) still has a landing slot.
export type BlockIntervalEvents
	// Flat (rangeIdx, startPos, endPos) triples, sliced per block by `base`.
	export var rangeIdx as RegIntArray
	export var startPos as RegIntArray
	export var endPos as RegIntArray
	// base[blockId] is the flat-array offset of block's first event; sized to
	// numBlockSlots+1 so base[blockId+1] is always the slice end.
	export var base as RegIntArray

	export static function build(ranges LiveRangeArray, blockMaxPos RegIntArray) returns BlockIntervalEvents
		let numBlockSlots = blockMaxPos.count()
		let numRanges = ranges.count()

		// Pass 1: per-block event counts, so we can prefix-sum into slice offsets
		// and fill the flat arrays positionally without per-block dynamic growth.
		var counts = RegIntArray.create()
		var ci = 0
		while ci < numBlockSlots 'initCounts'
			counts.push(0)
			ci = ci + 1
		end 'initCounts'

		var ri = 0
		while ri < numRanges 'countRange'
			let range = try ranges.get(ri) otherwise panic("BlockIntervalEvents.build: ri < numRanges but ranges.get({ri}) failed")
			for iv in range.intervals 'eachInterval'
				if eventIsLive(iv, blockMaxPos: blockMaxPos, numBlockSlots: numBlockSlots) 'keep'
					let prev = try counts.get(iv.blockId) otherwise panic("invariant: counts.get({iv.blockId}) OOB; eventIsLive bounds-checked blockId")
					try counts.set(iv.blockId, value: prev + 1) otherwise panic("invariant: counts.set OOB")
				end 'keep'
			end 'eachInterval'
			ri = ri + 1
		end 'countRange'

		// Prefix-sum counts into base offsets (one extra entry for the final end).
		var base = RegIntArray.create()
		var total = 0
		var bi = 0
		while bi < numBlockSlots 'initBase'
			base.push(total)
			let c = try counts.get(bi) otherwise panic("invariant: counts.get({bi}) OOB during base")
			total = total + c
			bi = bi + 1
		end 'initBase'
		base.push(total)

		// Pass 2: fill the flat triple arrays. `cursor[blockId]` tracks the next
		// free slot in each block's slice.
		var rangeIdxArr = RegIntArray.create()
		var startPosArr = RegIntArray.create()
		var endPosArr = RegIntArray.create()
		var fi = 0
		while fi < total 'initFlat'
			rangeIdxArr.push(0)
			startPosArr.push(0)
			endPosArr.push(0)
			fi = fi + 1
		end 'initFlat'

		var cursor = RegIntArray.create()
		var cu = 0
		while cu < numBlockSlots 'initCursor'
			let b0 = try base.get(cu) otherwise panic("invariant: base.get({cu}) OOB during cursor init")
			cursor.push(b0)
			cu = cu + 1
		end 'initCursor'

		var ri2 = 0
		while ri2 < numRanges 'fillRange'
			let range = try ranges.get(ri2) otherwise panic("BlockIntervalEvents.build: ri2 < numRanges but ranges.get({ri2}) failed")
			for iv in range.intervals 'eachInterval2'
				if eventIsLive(iv, blockMaxPos: blockMaxPos, numBlockSlots: numBlockSlots) 'keep2'
					let maxPos = try blockMaxPos.get(iv.blockId) otherwise panic("invariant: blockMaxPos.get({iv.blockId}) OOB; eventIsLive bounds-checked")
					var endIdx = iv.endPos
					if endIdx > maxPos + 1 'clampEnd'
						endIdx = maxPos + 1
					end 'clampEnd'
					let slot = try cursor.get(iv.blockId) otherwise panic("invariant: cursor.get({iv.blockId}) OOB")
					try rangeIdxArr.set(slot, value: ri2) otherwise panic("invariant: rangeIdxArr.set OOB")
					try startPosArr.set(slot, value: iv.startPos) otherwise panic("invariant: startPosArr.set OOB")
					try endPosArr.set(slot, value: endIdx) otherwise panic("invariant: endPosArr.set OOB")
					try cursor.set(iv.blockId, value: slot + 1) otherwise panic("invariant: cursor.set OOB")
				end 'keep2'
			end 'eachInterval2'
			ri2 = ri2 + 1
		end 'fillRange'

		return Self{rangeIdx: rangeIdxArr, startPos: startPosArr, endPos: endPosArr, base: base}
	end 'build'

	// Slice start for `blockId`'s events.
	export function sliceStart(blockId BlockId) returns RegInt
		return try base.get(blockId) otherwise panic("BlockIntervalEvents.sliceStart: base.get({blockId}) OOB")
	end 'sliceStart'

	// Slice end (exclusive) for `blockId`'s events.
	export function sliceEnd(blockId BlockId) returns RegInt
		return try base.get(blockId + 1) otherwise panic("BlockIntervalEvents.sliceEnd: base.get({blockId + 1}) OOB")
	end 'sliceEnd'
end 'BlockIntervalEvents'

// Shared keep-filter for a single interval event, byte-identical to the guards
// the two sweeps applied inline: in a block that exists in this func, non-empty,
// startPos in [0, maxPos+1]. Lifts the duplicated test into one place so the
// count pass and the fill pass cannot drift.
function eventIsLive(iv Interval, blockMaxPos RegIntArray, numBlockSlots RegInt) returns bool
	if iv.blockId < 0 or iv.blockId >= numBlockSlots 'badBlock'
		return false
	end 'badBlock'
	let maxPos = try blockMaxPos.get(iv.blockId) otherwise panic("invariant: eventIsLive blockMaxPos.get({iv.blockId}) OOB; just bounds-checked")
	if maxPos < 0 'notInFunc'
		return false
	end 'notInFunc'
	if iv.startPos >= iv.endPos 'emptyInterval'
		return false
	end 'emptyInterval'
	if iv.startPos < 0 or iv.startPos > maxPos + 1 'badStart'
		return false
	end 'badStart'
	return true
end 'eventIsLive'

// True if a RegClass is the FP class. Mirrors the gpr/fp discrimination used
// throughout the allocator (LocalSplitter's poolSizeFor pattern).
function regClassIsFp(regClass RegClass) returns bool
	return match regClass 'rc'
		gpr gives false
		fp gives true
	end 'rc'
end 'regClassIsFp'

// True if `range` belongs to the given register class.
function rangeIsClass(range LiveRange, regClass RegClass) returns bool
	return regClassIsFp(range.regClass) == regClassIsFp(regClass)
end 'rangeIsClass'

// Compute peak register-pressure demand per class across the whole function,
// measured the way the colorer allocates: per disjoint sub-pool, with fixed
// pseudo-ranges counted by DISTINCT physical register rather than by raw range
// count. See MaxLiveResult for why the old single "MaxLive vs k" total both
// over-stated pressure at call sites and hid callee-saved over-subscription.
//
// Per (block, position) we hold the set of live ranges of the class (an event-
// driven enter/exit sweep keyed off each interval's [startPos, endPos), the
// same half-open convention as rangeLiveAt) and derive:
//   * total demand    = live virtuals + |distinct registers the live fixed
//                        pseudo-ranges occupy|.
//   * callee demand    = live crossesCall virtuals + |distinct CALLEE-saved
//                        registers the live fixed pseudo-ranges occupy|.
// The running max of each over all positions/blocks per class is the result.
//
// Fixed pseudo-ranges (fixedReg != RM_NONE) come from emitClobberRanges /
// emitFixedRegRanges / emitPerBitParamRanges (regClass gpr/fp); they pin real
// registers at the call/arg-setup windows. Reading pressure off `ranges` (not
// a liveIn/liveOut walk) is required because the pseudo-ranges live only here.
// Per-position enter/exit range-index buckets for one block, indexed by
// position (0..maxPos+1). `enters[p]` holds the range indices whose interval
// starts at p; `exits[p]` those whose (clamped) interval end is p. Consumed by
// the linear-scan sweep in computeClassDemand / pickForClass.
type PositionEventBuckets
	export var enters as RegIntArrayArray
	export var exits as RegIntArrayArray

	export static function create(enters RegIntArrayArray, exits RegIntArrayArray) returns PositionEventBuckets
		return Self{enters: enters, exits: exits}
	end 'create'
end 'PositionEventBuckets'

// Scatter `blockId`'s precomputed interval events into per-position enter/exit
// buckets (positions 1..maxPos; endPos can reach maxPos+1, so the arrays are
// sized to maxPos+2 to land that exit). Reads only the block's own event slice,
// so this is O(block events), replacing the former O(numRanges) per-block scan.
function buildPositionEventBuckets(events BlockIntervalEvents, blockId BlockId, maxPos RegInt) returns PositionEventBuckets
	var entersAt = RegIntArrayArray.create()
	var exitsAt = RegIntArrayArray.create()
	var ei = 0
	while ei <= maxPos + 1 'initEvents'
		entersAt.push(RegIntArray.create())
		exitsAt.push(RegIntArray.create())
		ei = ei + 1
	end 'initEvents'

	let lo = events.sliceStart(blockId)
	let hi = events.sliceEnd(blockId)
	var e = lo
	while e < hi 'eachEvent'
		let ri = try events.rangeIdx.get(e) otherwise panic("invariant: events.rangeIdx.get({e}) OOB in slice")
		let sp = try events.startPos.get(e) otherwise panic("invariant: events.startPos.get({e}) OOB in slice")
		let ep = try events.endPos.get(e) otherwise panic("invariant: events.endPos.get({e}) OOB in slice")
		var enterBucket = try entersAt.get(sp) otherwise panic("invariant: entersAt sized to maxPos+2 but get({sp}) failed")
		enterBucket.push(ri)
		var exitBucket = try exitsAt.get(ep) otherwise panic("invariant: exitsAt sized to maxPos+2 but get({ep}) failed")
		exitBucket.push(ri)
		e = e + 1
	end 'eachEvent'

	return PositionEventBuckets.create(entersAt, exits: exitsAt)
end 'buildPositionEventBuckets'

export function computeMaxLivePerBlock(ranges LiveRangeArray, module TargetModule, func IrFunction, desc TargetRegAlloc) returns MaxLiveResult
	// Per-block interval events bucketed ONCE (class-independent — the
	// per-position sweep filters by class). Shared across both class passes so
	// the old per-block × all-ranges scan happens a single time, not 2 × blocks.
	let blockMaxPos = blockMaxPositions(module, func: func)
	let events = BlockIntervalEvents.build(ranges, blockMaxPos: blockMaxPos)
	let gpr = computeClassDemand(ranges, regClass: RegClass.gpr, desc: desc, blockMaxPos: blockMaxPos, events: events)
	let fp = computeClassDemand(ranges, regClass: RegClass.fp, desc: desc, blockMaxPos: blockMaxPos, events: events)
	return MaxLiveResult.create(gpr.total, fp: fp.total, gprCallee: gpr.callee, fpCallee: fp.callee)
end 'computeMaxLivePerBlock'

// Peak (total, callee) demand for one class. Pulled out of computeMaxLivePerBlock
// so the two classes share one event-sweep implementation.
type ClassDemand
	export var total as RegInt
	export var callee as RegInt

	export static function create(total RegInt, callee RegInt) returns ClassDemand
		return Self{total: total, callee: callee}
	end 'create'
end 'ClassDemand'

// Incremental sub-pool demand counters maintained DURING the per-block live-set
// sweep, so the demand at each position is O(1) instead of an O(liveSet) rescan
// with a per-position scratch allocation. The single-class event sweep
// (computeClassDemand / pickForClass) calls `enter`/`exit` as ranges become
// live/dead and `markChosen` when the picker commits a spill; `total()` /
// `callee()` then read the current demand directly. Equivalent to liveDemand's
// per-position recompute, but the work is paid once per interval event rather
// than once per position.
//
// Demand is measured the way the colorer allocates (see MaxLiveResult):
//   total  = live not-chosen virtuals + |distinct registers live fixed ranges pin|
//   callee = live not-chosen crossesCall virtuals + |distinct CALLEE-saved registers
//            live fixed ranges pin|
// Fixed ranges are deduplicated by register via `fixedRefCount` (a register's
// distinct contribution is counted while >= 1 fixed range pins it).
type DemandTracker
	// `calleeByOrdinal[ord]` true iff `ord` is a callee-saved register of the
	// class (parallel to the register ordinal space, sized regOrdCap). Precomputed
	// once per class pass so enter/exit need no per-event class lookup.
	export var calleeByOrdinal as BoolArray
	// Per-register count of currently-live fixed ranges pinned to that ordinal.
	export var fixedRefCount as RegIntArray
	export var liveVirtuals as RegInt
	export var liveCalleeVirtuals as RegInt
	export var distinctFixed as RegInt
	export var distinctCalleeFixed as RegInt

	export static function create(regClass RegClass, regOrdCap RegInt, desc TargetRegAlloc) returns DemandTracker
		var calleeByOrdinal = BoolArray.create()
		var fixedRefCount = RegIntArray.create()
		var i = 0
		while i < regOrdCap 'init'
			calleeByOrdinal.push(ordinalIsCalleeSaved(i, regClass: regClass, desc: desc))
			fixedRefCount.push(0)
			i = i + 1
		end 'init'
		return Self{calleeByOrdinal: calleeByOrdinal, fixedRefCount: fixedRefCount, liveVirtuals: 0, liveCalleeVirtuals: 0, distinctFixed: 0, distinctCalleeFixed: 0}
	end 'create'

	// Zero all running counts for the start of a new block. `calleeByOrdinal`
	// (class-constant) is preserved. Needed because ranges live past a block's
	// last swept position are never `exit`ed, so their contributions must be
	// cleared explicitly rather than balanced out.
	export function reset()
		liveVirtuals = 0
		liveCalleeVirtuals = 0
		distinctFixed = 0
		distinctCalleeFixed = 0
		var i = 0
		let n = fixedRefCount.count()
		while i < n 'clear'
			try fixedRefCount.set(i, value: 0) otherwise panic("invariant: fixedRefCount.set OOB in reset")
			i = i + 1
		end 'clear'
	end 'reset'

	export function total() returns RegInt
		return liveVirtuals + distinctFixed
	end 'total'

	export function callee() returns RegInt
		return liveCalleeVirtuals + distinctCalleeFixed
	end 'callee'

	// Account a range becoming live. `chosen` lets virtuals already spilled this
	// round be excluded from the live demand (they relieve every position).
	export function enter(range LiveRange, chosen BoolArray)
		if range.fixedReg != RM_NONE 'fixed'
			let ord = range.fixedReg
			if ord >= 0 and ord < fixedRefCount.count() 'inRange'
				let prev = try fixedRefCount.get(ord) otherwise panic("invariant: fixedRefCount.get OOB in enter")
				try fixedRefCount.set(ord, value: prev + 1) otherwise panic("invariant: fixedRefCount.set OOB in enter")
				if prev == 0 'firstPin'
					distinctFixed = distinctFixed + 1
					let isCallee = try calleeByOrdinal.get(ord) otherwise false
					if isCallee 'callee'
						distinctCalleeFixed = distinctCalleeFixed + 1
					end 'callee'
				end 'firstPin'
			end 'inRange'
		end 'fixed' else 'virtual'
			let isChosen = try chosen.get(range.valueId) otherwise false
			if not isChosen 'counted'
				liveVirtuals = liveVirtuals + 1
				if range.crossesCall 'cross'
					liveCalleeVirtuals = liveCalleeVirtuals + 1
				end 'cross'
			end 'counted'
		end 'virtual'
	end 'enter'

	// Account a range becoming dead — exact inverse of `enter`. The `chosen`
	// state of a virtual is stable between its enter and exit at one position
	// EXCEPT when markChosen fired in between; markChosen already removed it from
	// the live counts, and a chosen virtual is skipped here too, so the counts
	// stay balanced.
	export function exit(range LiveRange, chosen BoolArray)
		if range.fixedReg != RM_NONE 'fixed'
			let ord = range.fixedReg
			if ord >= 0 and ord < fixedRefCount.count() 'inRange'
				let prev = try fixedRefCount.get(ord) otherwise panic("invariant: fixedRefCount.get OOB in exit")
				try fixedRefCount.set(ord, value: prev - 1) otherwise panic("invariant: fixedRefCount.set OOB in exit")
				if prev == 1 'lastPin'
					distinctFixed = distinctFixed - 1
					let isCallee = try calleeByOrdinal.get(ord) otherwise false
					if isCallee 'callee'
						distinctCalleeFixed = distinctCalleeFixed - 1
					end 'callee'
				end 'lastPin'
			end 'inRange'
		end 'fixed' else 'virtual'
			let isChosen = try chosen.get(range.valueId) otherwise false
			if not isChosen 'counted'
				liveVirtuals = liveVirtuals - 1
				if range.crossesCall 'cross'
					liveCalleeVirtuals = liveCalleeVirtuals - 1
				end 'cross'
			end 'counted'
		end 'virtual'
	end 'exit'

	// Account a still-live virtual being chosen to spill: it stops contributing
	// to demand from now on. Called by the picker right after commitSpill so the
	// relief loop sees demand shrink. (Fixed ranges are never chosen.)
	export function markChosen(range LiveRange)
		liveVirtuals = liveVirtuals - 1
		if range.crossesCall 'cross'
			liveCalleeVirtuals = liveCalleeVirtuals - 1
		end 'cross'
	end 'markChosen'
end 'DemandTracker'

function computeClassDemand(ranges LiveRangeArray, regClass RegClass, desc TargetRegAlloc, blockMaxPos RegIntArray, events BlockIntervalEvents) returns ClassDemand
	let numBlockSlots = blockMaxPos.count()
	let numRanges = ranges.count()
	let regOrdCap = maxPoolOrdinalFor(regClass, desc: desc) + 1

	var maxTotal = 0
	var maxCallee = 0

	// Empty `chosen` set: pure pressure measurement spills nothing, so every
	// `chosen.get` returns the false fallback.
	let noneChosen = BoolArray.create()

	// Incremental demand counters, updated as ranges enter/exit the sweep so the
	// per-position demand is O(1). Reset at each block (ranges live past a block's
	// last position are never exited).
	var tracker = DemandTracker.create(regClass, regOrdCap: regOrdCap, desc: desc)

	// Range-index -> slot in `liveSet`, or -1 when not live. Allocated once for
	// the whole pass; entered ranges are reset to -1 after each block.
	var liveSlot = RegIntArray.create()
	var si = 0
	while si < numRanges 'initSlot'
		liveSlot.push(-1)
		si = si + 1
	end 'initSlot'

	var b = 0
	while b < numBlockSlots 'eachBlock'
		let maxPos = try blockMaxPos.get(b) otherwise panic("computeClassDemand: b < count by guard but get({b}) failed")
		if maxPos < 0 'notInFunc'
			b = b + 1
			continue
		end 'notInFunc'

		// Per-position enter/exit event buckets for this block, filled from the
		// block's precomputed event slice (O(block events) instead of the old
		// O(numRanges) per-block scan).
		let buckets = buildPositionEventBuckets(events, blockId: b, maxPos: maxPos)
		let entersAt = buckets.enters
		let exitsAt = buckets.exits

		var liveSet = RegIntArray.create()
		tracker.reset()

		// Sweep from position 0, not 1: live-in / live-through intervals have
		// startPos == 0 (buildIntervalsForValue), so their enter events sit in
		// entersAt[0]. Starting at 1 never applied those enters, leaving every
		// value that flows INTO a block invisible to the demand count for the
		// whole block — an undercount that let genuinely over-pressured blocks
		// read "within budget", so the colorer (whose interference graph counts
		// position 0) then couldn't color and the reactive loop force-spilled.
		// applyExits(exitsAt[0]) is a no-op (min endPos is 1), so p=0 only adds
		// the position-0 enters, matching the interference graph exactly.
		var p = 0
		while p <= maxPos 'eachPos'
			applyExits(liveSet, liveSlot: liveSlot, exitBucket: try exitsAt.get(p) otherwise panic("invariant: exitsAt get({p}) failed"), ranges: ranges, regClass: regClass, tracker: tracker, chosen: noneChosen)
			applyEnters(liveSet, liveSlot: liveSlot, enterBucket: try entersAt.get(p) otherwise panic("invariant: entersAt get({p}) failed"), ranges: ranges, regClass: regClass, tracker: tracker, chosen: noneChosen)

			if tracker.total() > maxTotal 'newTotal'
				maxTotal = tracker.total()
			end 'newTotal'
			if tracker.callee() > maxCallee 'newCallee'
				maxCallee = tracker.callee()
			end 'newCallee'

			p = p + 1
		end 'eachPos'

		for idx in liveSet 'resetLive'
			try liveSlot.set(idx, value: -1) otherwise panic("invariant: liveSlot.set OOB during reset; sized to numRanges")
		end 'resetLive'

		b = b + 1
	end 'eachBlock'

	return ClassDemand.create(maxTotal, callee: maxCallee)
end 'computeClassDemand'

// How far a measured demand exceeds its budget (0 when within budget). Used by
// the Belady driver to fold the four sub-pool demands (gpr/fp total and callee)
// into a single over-budget magnitude that must strictly shrink each round.
export function pressureExcess(demand RegInt, budget RegInt) returns RegInt
	if demand > budget 'over'
		return demand - budget
	end 'over'
	return 0
end 'pressureExcess'

// True if `range` is live at (blockId, pos): half-open [startPos, endPos)
// overlap, same convention as rangesInterfere / buildInterferenceGraph.
function rangeLiveAt(range LiveRange, blockId BlockId, pos RegInt) returns bool
	for iv in range.intervals 'each'
		if iv.blockId == blockId and iv.startPos <= pos and pos < iv.endPos 'live'
			return true
		end 'live'
	end 'each'
	return false
end 'rangeLiveAt'

// True if `range` has an interval in `blockId` (used to test whether a range
// is live-in toward a successor block — its presence in the successor's
// interval list means it flows there).
function rangeLiveInBlock(range LiveRange, blockId BlockId) returns bool
	for iv in range.intervals 'each'
		if iv.blockId == blockId 'present'
			return true
		end 'present'
	end 'each'
	return false
end 'rangeLiveInBlock'

// ============================================================
// Next-use analysis
// ============================================================

// Precomputed, once per round, the first read position of every value as a
// (blockId, position) pair. We avoid the per-point forward scan called out as
// a hotspot in review by building this per-valueId next-use map from a single
// forward read scan, then consulting it O(1) per (point, range).
//
// `firstReadBlock[vid]` / `firstReadPos[vid]`: the (block, position) of the
// FIRST op (RPO order) that reads vid. -1 if never read (dead value). This is
// a global "next use" approximation: combined with the per-point distance
// computation it yields a monotone ordering good enough for MIN. Correctness
// needs only MaxLive <= k; next-use only governs WHICH value to spill.
type NextUseMap
	export var firstReadBlock as RegIntArray
	export var firstReadPos as RegIntArray

	export static function create() returns NextUseMap
		return Self{firstReadBlock: RegIntArray.create(), firstReadPos: RegIntArray.create()}
	end 'create'
end 'NextUseMap'

// Build the next-use map by walking blocks in RPO order and, within each
// block, ops front-to-back. The first time a value is seen as a read it is
// stamped; later reads are ignored (we want the earliest). Branch-edge arg
// sources count as a read at the predecessor's terminator slot.
function buildNextUseMap(ranges LiveRangeArray, module TargetModule, func IrFunction, rpo RpoInfo, regTarget RegAllocTarget) returns NextUseMap
	var map = NextUseMap.create()

	var maxVid = 0
	for range in ranges 'findMax'
		if range.valueId > maxVid 'higher'
			maxVid = range.valueId
		end 'higher'
	end 'findMax'

	var i = 0
	while i <= maxVid 'init'
		map.firstReadBlock.push(-1)
		map.firstReadPos.push(-1)
		i = i + 1
	end 'init'

	let numOrder = rpo.order.count()
	var oi = 0
	while oi < numOrder 'eachRpoBlock'
		let blockId = try rpo.order.get(oi) otherwise panic("buildNextUseMap: oi < count by guard but rpo.order.get({oi}) failed")
		let block = findBlockById(module, func: func, blockId: blockId)

		var opIdx = 0
		for packed in block.opRefs 'eachOp'
			var reads = RegIntArray.create()
			regTarget.countOpReads(module, reads: reads, packed: packed)
			recordFirstReads(map, reads: reads, blockId: blockId, pos: opIdx + 1, maxVid: maxVid)
			opIdx = opIdx + 1
		end 'eachOp'

		if block.hasTerminatorOp() 'hasTerm'
			var reads = RegIntArray.create()
			regTarget.countOpReads(module, reads: reads, packed: block.terminatorIndex())
			recordFirstReads(map, reads: reads, blockId: blockId, pos: opIdx + 1, maxVid: maxVid)
		end 'hasTerm'

		// Branch-edge arg sources: a value used as a block-arg source is read
		// at the predecessor's terminator slot. Position opRefs.count()+1 is
		// the terminator slot.
		let termPos = block.opRefs.count() + 1
		for edge in block.branchEdges 'eachEdge'
			recordFirstReads(map, reads: edge.argIds, blockId: blockId, pos: termPos, maxVid: maxVid)
		end 'eachEdge'

		oi = oi + 1
	end 'eachRpoBlock'

	return map
end 'buildNextUseMap'

// Stamp the first-read (block, pos) for each id in `reads` that hasn't been
// seen yet. Only ids within [0, maxVid] are recorded.
function recordFirstReads(map NextUseMap, reads RegIntArray, blockId BlockId, pos RegInt, maxVid RegInt)
	for vid in reads 'each'
		if vid < 0 or vid > maxVid 'outOfRange'
			continue
		end 'outOfRange'
		let prev = try map.firstReadBlock.get(vid) otherwise panic("recordFirstReads: vid in range but firstReadBlock.get failed")
		if prev < 0 'unset'
			try map.firstReadBlock.set(vid, value: blockId) otherwise panic("invariant: firstReadBlock.set OOB")
			try map.firstReadPos.set(vid, value: pos) otherwise panic("invariant: firstReadPos.set OOB")
		end 'unset'
	end 'each'
end 'recordFirstReads'

// Distance from point (blockId, fromPos) to the next use of `range`, using
// the precomputed NextUseMap and the RPO ordering for the cross-block term.
// Larger = farther = better spill candidate (Belady spills farthest-next-use).
//
//   1. Next use is in THIS block after fromPos  -> distance = readPos - fromPos.
//   2. Value is live out toward a successor (has an interval in a successor
//      block) -> distance = (blockMaxPos[B] - fromPos) + rpoIndexOfNextLiveBlock
//      * BLOCK_DISTANCE_UNIT, so survival farther down the RPO chain sorts as
//      farther while staying above any intra-block distance.
//   3. No use at or beyond this point (dead here) -> NEXT_USE_INFINITE.
function nextUseFromPoint(range LiveRange, blockId BlockId, fromPos RegInt, rpo RpoInfo, nextUse NextUseMap, blockMaxPos RegIntArray, cfg CfgInfo) returns RegInt
	let vid = range.valueId

	// Case 1: in-block use after fromPos.
	let readBlock = getOr(nextUse.firstReadBlock, index: vid, fallback: -1)
	let readPos = getOr(nextUse.firstReadPos, index: vid, fallback: -1)
	if readBlock == blockId and readPos > fromPos 'inBlockUse'
		return readPos - fromPos
	end 'inBlockUse'

	// Case 2: live-out toward a successor. Find the min RPO index among
	// successors in whose interval list `range` appears live.
	let maxPos = getOr(blockMaxPos, index: blockId, fallback: 0)
	let succs = try cfg.successors.get(blockId) otherwise 'noSuccs'
		return NEXT_USE_INFINITE
	end 'noSuccs'

	var bestRpo = i64.max
	for succ in succs 'eachSucc'
		if rangeLiveInBlock(range, blockId: succ) 'liveThere'
			let ri = getOr(rpo.index, index: succ, fallback: i64.max)
			if ri < bestRpo 'closer'
				bestRpo = ri
			end 'closer'
		end 'liveThere'
	end 'eachSucc'

	if bestRpo == i64.max 'noLiveSucc'
		// Dead after this point (no in-block use, no live successor).
		return NEXT_USE_INFINITE
	end 'noLiveSucc'

	return (maxPos - fromPos) + bestRpo * BLOCK_DISTANCE_UNIT
end 'nextUseFromPoint'

// ============================================================
// Block-arg plumbing identification (W-set safety)
// ============================================================

// Build a bitmap (indexed by valueId) of every value involved in block-arg
// (phi) plumbing: both the block-arg DESTINATIONS (phi-merge values) and the
// branch-edge SOURCES that feed them. Belady must NOT spill any of these.
//
// Why both ends are off-limits (not just destinations):
//   A block-arg destination has multiple incoming SSA sources (one per
//   predecessor). insertSpillCode's two-pass branch-edge handling
//   (remapBranchEdgeArgs + the successor spill-store) is only consistent when
//   either the destination AND all its sources are spilled, or none are (the
//   memory-routed-phi shortcut — which is currently gated off). Spilling a
//   destination while a source stays in a register, OR spilling a source that
//   feeds a destination whose slot is coalesced with the source's slot,
//   produces a parallel-copy / spill-store mismatch: the value arrives in one
//   place but is read from another.
//
//   The W-set fixpoint from Braun/Hack would reconcile this by forcing all
//   sources spilled when a destination is, but that depends on the gated-off
//   memory-routed-phi path being sound. The conservative-but-correct rule —
//   and the one that keeps Belady purely a pressure-relief pass with no spill
//   emission of its own — is to leave block-arg plumbing values to the
//   reactive loop, which already owns that machinery. Ordinary cross-block
//   and intra-block temporaries (the bulk of register pressure) remain
//   freely spillable; their reload/store plumbing stays clear of the phi
//   parallel-copy machinery.
export function buildBlockArgPlumbingSet(module TargetModule, func IrFunction) returns BoolArray
	var maxVid = 0
	for blockRef in func.blockRefs 'findMax'
		let block = try module.blocks.get(blockRef) otherwise panic("invariant: blockRef from func.blockRefs not in module.blocks")
		for arg in block.blockArgs 'eachArg'
			if arg.valueId > maxVid 'higherArg'
				maxVid = arg.valueId
			end 'higherArg'
		end 'eachArg'
		for edge in block.branchEdges 'eachEdge'
			for srcId in edge.argIds 'eachSrc'
				if srcId > maxVid 'higherSrc'
					maxVid = srcId
				end 'higherSrc'
			end 'eachSrc'
		end 'eachEdge'
	end 'findMax'

	var result = BoolArray.create()
	var i = 0
	while i <= maxVid 'init'
		result.push(false)
		i = i + 1
	end 'init'

	for blockRef in func.blockRefs 'eachBlock'
		let block = try module.blocks.get(blockRef) otherwise panic("invariant: blockRef from func.blockRefs not in module.blocks")
		for arg in block.blockArgs 'markArg'
			try result.set(arg.valueId, value: true) otherwise panic("invariant: buildBlockArgPlumbingSet.set OOB; sized to maxVid+1")
		end 'markArg'
		for edge in block.branchEdges 'markEdge'
			for srcId in edge.argIds 'markSrc'
				if srcId >= 0 'validSrc'
					try result.set(srcId, value: true) otherwise panic("invariant: buildBlockArgPlumbingSet.set OOB source; sized to maxVid+1")
				end 'validSrc'
			end 'markSrc'
		end 'markEdge'
	end 'eachBlock'

	return result
end 'buildBlockArgPlumbingSet'

// True if `range` is a legal Belady spill candidate of class `regClass`:
//   - right register class,
//   - not a fixed pseudo-range (those are physical constraints — they count
//     toward pressure but can never get a stack slot),
//   - finite spill weight (reload vregs and phi-merge sub-ranges are
//     SPILL_WEIGHT_INFINITE — already unspillable),
//   - not a block-arg plumbing value (dest or source; W-set safety — also
//     covers entry-block parameters, which have no def op to anchor a store),
//   - not already chosen this round.
//
// Cross-block (multi-interval) values ARE spillable: insertSpillCode stores
// after the def and reloads before each use, with the cross-block-arg case
// handled by remapBranchEdgeArgs. The dense-function pressure that walls the
// self-compile is dominated by cross-block values, so excluding them would
// defeat the pass. Spilling a cross-block managed RETURN value is correct only
// because insertPhysicalConstraints keeps each return-register phys-dest write
// (mov x0,<retVal>; mov x1,<errorFlag>) live to the block terminator when no
// call follows it (see LiveRangeBuilder.insertPhysicalConstraints): the staged
// return register stays OCCUPIED through `ret`, so a reloaded return value (or
// a rematerialized error-flag constant) materialized just before the return
// movs interferes with the phys-dest and cannot be colored into the return
// register and clobber the already-staged value. Without that interference the
// colorer would assign the reload x0 and the function would return nil (the
// URL.resolve / multi-value-return nil-pointer miscompile).
export function isSpillCandidate(range LiveRange, regClass RegClass, blockArgPlumbing BoolArray, chosen BoolArray) returns bool
	if not rangeIsClass(range, regClass: regClass) 'wrongClass'
		return false
	end 'wrongClass'
	if range.fixedReg != RM_NONE 'fixed'
		return false
	end 'fixed'
	if range.spillWeight == SPILL_WEIGHT_INFINITE 'unspillable'
		return false
	end 'unspillable'
	let isBlockArg = try blockArgPlumbing.get(range.valueId) otherwise false
	if isBlockArg 'blockArg'
		return false
	end 'blockArg'
	let already = try chosen.get(range.valueId) otherwise false
	if already 'taken'
		return false
	end 'taken'
	return true
end 'isSpillCandidate'

// ============================================================
// Spill picker
// ============================================================

// Greedy Belady/MIN spill picker. For each over-pressured (block, position),
// of each register class, gather the live spillable ranges and select the
// `excess` of them with the FARTHEST next use, marking each chosen and
// pushing it into the returned SpillDecision. Both sub-pool constraints the
// colorer must satisfy are enforced per position (see relievePressureAt):
//
//   (a) CALLEE-saved: live call-crossing virtuals + distinct callee-pinned
//       fixed registers <= kCallee. crossesCall values can only use callee-
//       saved registers (caller-saved ones are clobbered by the call they
//       span), so this binds at EVERY position they are live, not only at the
//       call op. This is NOT an optional refinement: it is a hard coloring
//       constraint, and the one the old "total vs k" metric hid — a function
//       can sit at total <= k yet have far more call-crossing values than
//       callee-saved registers.
//   (b) TOTAL: live virtuals + distinct fixed registers <= k. Fixed pseudo-
//       ranges are counted by distinct physical register, which removes the
//       call-site over-count (overlapping same-register clobber / arg-setup
//       pins count once) that previously demanded unspillable "excess".
//
// Selection uses inline selection (no Array.sort), deterministic tie-break by
// LARGER valueId. Rematerializable values are pushed to spilledRanges like
// any other — Belady is a pressure-relief pass, not a cost-minimization pass;
// insertSpillCode decides remat-vs-stack downstream.
export function pickBeladySpills(ranges LiveRangeArray, module TargetModule, func IrFunction, rpo RpoInfo, cfg CfgInfo, regTarget RegAllocTarget, desc TargetRegAlloc) returns SpillDecision
	var decision = SpillDecision.create()

	let kGpr = poolSizeFor(RegClass.gpr, desc: desc)
	let kFp = poolSizeFor(RegClass.fp, desc: desc)
	let kCalleeGpr = calleeSavedSizeFor(RegClass.gpr, desc: desc)
	let kCalleeFp = calleeSavedSizeFor(RegClass.fp, desc: desc)

	let blockMaxPos = blockMaxPositions(module, func: func)
	let blockArgPlumbing = buildBlockArgPlumbingSet(module, func: func)
	let nextUse = buildNextUseMap(ranges, module: module, func: func, rpo: rpo, regTarget: regTarget)
	// Per-block interval events bucketed ONCE and shared across both class
	// passes, the same single-pass technique computeMaxLivePerBlock uses — the
	// former per-block × all-ranges scan was the spill picker's quadratic wall.
	let events = BlockIntervalEvents.build(ranges, blockMaxPos: blockMaxPos)

	// `chosen` carries forward across all positions and blocks within this
	// round: once a value is selected to spill, it relieves every position it
	// was live at, so subsequent positions must not re-select it.
	var chosen = BoolArray.create()
	var maxVid = 0
	for range in ranges 'findMax'
		if range.valueId > maxVid 'higher'
			maxVid = range.valueId
		end 'higher'
	end 'findMax'
	var ci = 0
	while ci <= maxVid 'initChosen'
		chosen.push(false)
		ci = ci + 1
	end 'initChosen'

	pickForClass(ranges, regClass: RegClass.gpr, k: kGpr, kCallee: kCalleeGpr, blockMaxPos: blockMaxPos, blockArgPlumbing: blockArgPlumbing, nextUse: nextUse, chosen: chosen, decision: decision, rpo: rpo, cfg: cfg, desc: desc, events: events)
	pickForClass(ranges, regClass: RegClass.fp, k: kFp, kCallee: kCalleeFp, blockMaxPos: blockMaxPos, blockArgPlumbing: blockArgPlumbing, nextUse: nextUse, chosen: chosen, decision: decision, rpo: rpo, cfg: cfg, desc: desc, events: events)

	return decision
end 'pickBeladySpills'

// Pick spills for one register class over all blocks/positions. Greedy across
// each block carrying `chosen` forward, so a single chosen spill at a block's
// worst position relieves the whole contiguous run.
//
// Per block we run a classic linear-scan sweep that maintains the SET of range
// indices actually live at the current position, instead of rescanning all
// ranges at every position (the old O(positions x allRanges) wall: ~22270
// ranges, ~15000 of them 1-position clobber pseudo-ranges, scanned per pos).
// The sweep is event-driven off each range's interval(s) IN THIS BLOCK:
//
//   * enter at startPos, exit at endPos, matching rangeLiveAt's half-open
//     convention exactly (a range is live at pos iff some interval in this
//     block has startPos <= pos < endPos). At each position p we first apply
//     exits where endPos == p (those died strictly before p), then enters where
//     startPos == p, so `liveSet` membership equals rangeLiveAt(range, b, p)
//     for every range at every p.
//   * the 1-position clobber pseudo-ranges have interval [callPos, callPos+1):
//     they enter at callPos and exit at callPos+1, so they inflate pressure
//     ONLY at their exact call position and are gone by the next — handled by
//     the event sweep, never a full-array scan.
//
// `liveSet` is sized O(pressure) (a few dozen), so the per-position relief now
// scans the live set, not all ranges. `liveSlot` maps a range index to its
// slot in `liveSet` (or -1 when not live) for O(1) swap-remove on exit; it is
// allocated once for the whole class pass and only the entries this block
// touched are reset between blocks.
function pickForClass(ranges LiveRangeArray, regClass RegClass, k RegInt, kCallee RegInt, blockMaxPos RegIntArray, blockArgPlumbing BoolArray, nextUse NextUseMap, chosen BoolArray, decision SpillDecision, rpo RpoInfo, cfg CfgInfo, desc TargetRegAlloc, events BlockIntervalEvents)
	let numBlockSlots = blockMaxPos.count()
	let numRanges = ranges.count()
	let regOrdCap = maxPoolOrdinalFor(regClass, desc: desc) + 1

	// Incremental sub-pool demand, kept in sync with the live set by applyEnters /
	// applyExits and by relievePressureAt's markChosen on each commit, so the
	// per-position relief reads demand in O(1) instead of rescanning the live set.
	var tracker = DemandTracker.create(regClass, regOrdCap: regOrdCap, desc: desc)

	// Range-index -> slot in `liveSet`, or -1 when not live. Allocated once for
	// the whole class pass; entered ranges are reset to -1 after each block.
	var liveSlot = RegIntArray.create()
	var si = 0
	while si < numRanges 'initSlot'
		liveSlot.push(-1)
		si = si + 1
	end 'initSlot'

	var b = 0
	while b < numBlockSlots 'eachBlock'
		let maxPos = try blockMaxPos.get(b) otherwise panic("pickForClass: b < count by guard but get({b}) failed")
		if maxPos < 0 'notInFunc'
			b = b + 1
			continue
		end 'notInFunc'

		// Per-position enter/exit event buckets, filled from the block's
		// precomputed event slice (O(block events), not the old O(numRanges)
		// per-block scan). Positions run 1..maxPos; endPos can be maxPos+1, so
		// the arrays are sized to maxPos+2 to give that exit a landing slot (it
		// falls past the swept range and never fires, matching the old code
		// where such ranges stay live through maxPos).
		let buckets = buildPositionEventBuckets(events, blockId: b, maxPos: maxPos)
		let entersAt = buckets.enters
		let exitsAt = buckets.exits

		// Sweep positions, maintaining the live set. `liveSet` holds the range
		// indices live at the current position; `liveSlot[idx]` is its slot.
		var liveSet = RegIntArray.create()
		tracker.reset()

		// Start at position 0 so live-in / live-through ranges (startPos == 0)
		// enter the live set — see the matching note in computeClassDemand. The
		// spill picker must relieve at every position the demand tracker counts,
		// including position 0, or it would relieve against the same undercount.
		var p = 0
		while p <= maxPos 'eachPos'
			applyExits(liveSet, liveSlot: liveSlot, exitBucket: try exitsAt.get(p) otherwise panic("invariant: exitsAt get({p}) failed"), ranges: ranges, regClass: regClass, tracker: tracker, chosen: chosen)
			applyEnters(liveSet, liveSlot: liveSlot, enterBucket: try entersAt.get(p) otherwise panic("invariant: entersAt get({p}) failed"), ranges: ranges, regClass: regClass, tracker: tracker, chosen: chosen)

			relievePressureAt(ranges, liveSet: liveSet, regClass: regClass, blockId: b, pos: p, k: k, kCallee: kCallee, tracker: tracker, blockArgPlumbing: blockArgPlumbing, nextUse: nextUse, chosen: chosen, blockMaxPos: blockMaxPos, decision: decision, rpo: rpo, cfg: cfg)
			p = p + 1
		end 'eachPos'

		// Reset the touched `liveSlot` entries (ranges still live past maxPos
		// were never exited) so the next block starts from an all -1 map.
		for idx in liveSet 'resetLive'
			try liveSlot.set(idx, value: -1) otherwise panic("invariant: liveSlot.set OOB during reset; sized to numRanges")
		end 'resetLive'

		b = b + 1
	end 'eachBlock'
end 'pickForClass'

// Apply interval exits at the current position: each range in `exitBucket`
// dies strictly before this position (endPos == pos), so remove it from the
// live set via O(1) swap-remove keyed by its recorded slot and decrement the
// demand tracker. Only ranges of `tracker`'s class are tracked; others affect
// membership only.
function applyExits(liveSet RegIntArray, liveSlot RegIntArray, exitBucket RegIntArray, ranges LiveRangeArray, regClass RegClass, tracker DemandTracker, chosen BoolArray)
	for idx in exitBucket 'each'
		let slot = try liveSlot.get(idx) otherwise panic("invariant: liveSlot.get({idx}) OOB on exit")
		if slot < 0 'notLive'
			// Not currently live (e.g. another interval of the same range
			// already exited, or it never entered); nothing to remove.
			continue
		end 'notLive'
		let range = try ranges.get(idx) otherwise panic("invariant: liveSet idx OOB in ranges on exit")
		if rangeIsClass(range, regClass: regClass) 'sameClass'
			tracker.exit(range, chosen: chosen)
		end 'sameClass'
		let lastIdx = liveSet.count() - 1
		let moved = try liveSet.get(lastIdx) otherwise panic("invariant: liveSet non-empty when slot>=0 but get(last) failed")
		try liveSet.set(slot, value: moved) otherwise panic("invariant: liveSet.set OOB on swap-remove")
		try liveSlot.set(moved, value: slot) otherwise panic("invariant: liveSlot.set OOB for moved element")
		try liveSet.pop() otherwise panic("invariant: liveSet.pop on non-empty set")
		try liveSlot.set(idx, value: -1) otherwise panic("invariant: liveSlot.set(-1) OOB on exit")
	end 'each'
end 'applyExits'

// Apply interval enters at the current position: each range in `enterBucket`
// becomes live at this position (startPos == pos). Append to the live set,
// record its slot, and increment the demand tracker. Guards against double-enter
// (a range with two intervals in the same block both starting at pos would
// otherwise corrupt the slot map and double-count demand).
function applyEnters(liveSet RegIntArray, liveSlot RegIntArray, enterBucket RegIntArray, ranges LiveRangeArray, regClass RegClass, tracker DemandTracker, chosen BoolArray)
	for idx in enterBucket 'each'
		let slot = try liveSlot.get(idx) otherwise panic("invariant: liveSlot.get({idx}) OOB on enter")
		if slot >= 0 'alreadyLive'
			// Already live (overlapping/touching intervals of the same range in
			// this block); membership is unchanged.
			continue
		end 'alreadyLive'
		let range = try ranges.get(idx) otherwise panic("invariant: liveSet idx OOB in ranges on enter")
		if rangeIsClass(range, regClass: regClass) 'sameClass'
			tracker.enter(range, chosen: chosen)
		end 'sameClass'
		try liveSlot.set(idx, value: liveSet.count()) otherwise panic("invariant: liveSlot.set OOB on enter")
		liveSet.push(idx)
	end 'each'
end 'applyEnters'

// At one (block, pos), relieve BOTH sub-pool budgets the colorer must satisfy
// (see MaxLiveResult):
//
//   (a) CALLEE-saved: live call-crossing virtuals + distinct callee-pinned
//       fixed registers <= kCallee. A crossesCall value can ONLY live in a
//       callee-saved register (a caller-saved one is clobbered by the call it
//       spans), so this constraint binds at EVERY position the value is live,
//       not only at the call op. Relieved by spilling call-crossing values.
//
//   (b) TOTAL: live virtuals + distinct fixed registers <= k. Fixed pseudo-
//       ranges are deduplicated by physical register (an arg-setup phys-dest
//       and the call's clobber both pinning x0 consume ONE register, not two),
//       which removes the call-site over-count that made the old raw "live
//       count vs k" metric demand spills that can never help. Relieved by
//       spilling any spillable virtual.
//
// Callee relief runs FIRST: a call-crossing spill also reduces the total, so
// relieving the tighter sub-pool first avoids over-spilling for (b). Demand is
// read in O(1) from `tracker` (kept in sync by the sweep); each committed spill
// updates the tracker via markChosen so the loop sees demand shrink.
function relievePressureAt(ranges LiveRangeArray, liveSet RegIntArray, regClass RegClass, blockId BlockId, pos RegInt, k RegInt, kCallee RegInt, tracker DemandTracker, blockArgPlumbing BoolArray, nextUse NextUseMap, chosen BoolArray, blockMaxPos RegIntArray, decision SpillDecision, rpo RpoInfo, cfg CfgInfo)
	// (a) Callee-saved relief: do NOT spill call-crossing values — queue them
	// for splitting instead. A crossesCall value is callee-saved-only everywhere
	// it lives, so the only transform that relieves callee pressure is live-range
	// splitting around the call (store the short post-call piece to memory, keep
	// it out of a callee-saved register across the call) — NOT spilling the whole
	// value. Spilling a call-crossing value is counterproductive: its infinite-
	// weight reload still has to occupy a callee-saved register at the far-side
	// use, re-crossing the same call, so a cluster of such reloads exceeds the
	// callee-saved pool and reaches coloring unresolvable (the panic this fix
	// removes). commitSplit records the value in decision.splitRanges (NOT
	// spilledRanges, so no reload cluster is created) and marks it `chosen` so
	// the sweep's demand tracker drops it — modeling the relieved post-split
	// state. The splitting itself is performed by the reactive spill loop
	// (runSpillColorLoop), whose trySplitAtCall has a callee-saved-aware
	// pressure gate and an eviction-recolor backstop. runBeladyPressureReduction
	// detects pure callee over-subscription (nothing spillable for TOTAL relief)
	// and hands off to that loop.
	while tracker.callee() > kCallee 'splitForCallee'
		let picked = selectFarthest(ranges, liveSet: liveSet, regClass: regClass, blockId: blockId, pos: pos, calleeOnly: true, blockArgPlumbing: blockArgPlumbing, nextUse: nextUse, chosen: chosen, blockMaxPos: blockMaxPos, rpo: rpo, cfg: cfg)
		if not picked.found 'noCandidate'
			// Remaining callee excess is callee-pinned fixed / unspillable /
			// block-arg — architecture-limited; the reactive loop handles it.
			break
		end 'noCandidate'
		commitSplit(decision, range: picked.range, chosen: chosen)
		tracker.markChosen(picked.range)
	end 'splitForCallee'

	// (b) Total relief: reduce total distinct-register demand to fit the whole
	// pool. A picked virtual is relieved by SPILLING it ONLY when it does not
	// cross a call; a call-crossing pick is relieved by SPLITTING (commitSplit)
	// instead. This is the same invariant as phase (a), extended to the total
	// path: spilling ANY cross-call value re-creates the unresolvable cluster —
	// its reload still needs a callee-saved register at the far-side use and
	// re-crosses the call as a SPILL_WEIGHT_INFINITE range, and a crowd of such
	// reloads is uncolorable at iteration-0 BEFORE the reactive splitter (Pass
	// 1a trySplitAtCall) ever runs, so the split never gets a chance. Routing
	// the cross-call pick to commitSplit leaves it as a NORMAL-weight uncolored
	// range that the reactive loop's call-boundary splitter then resolves.
	while tracker.total() > k 'spillForTotal'
		let picked = selectFarthest(ranges, liveSet: liveSet, regClass: regClass, blockId: blockId, pos: pos, calleeOnly: false, blockArgPlumbing: blockArgPlumbing, nextUse: nextUse, chosen: chosen, blockMaxPos: blockMaxPos, rpo: rpo, cfg: cfg)
		if not picked.found 'noCandidate'
			// Remaining excess is fixed / unspillable / block-arg —
			// architecture-limited; the reactive loop handles it.
			break
		end 'noCandidate'
		if picked.range.crossesCall 'crossCall'
			commitSplit(decision, range: picked.range, chosen: chosen)
		end 'crossCall' else 'safeToSpill'
			commitSpill(decision, range: picked.range, chosen: chosen)
		end 'safeToSpill'
		tracker.markChosen(picked.range)
	end 'spillForTotal'
end 'relievePressureAt'

// Result of an inline farthest-next-use selection.
type PickResult
	export var found as bool
	export var range as LiveRange

	export static function create(found bool, range LiveRange) returns PickResult
		return Self{found: found, range: range}
	end 'create'
end 'PickResult'

// Inline selection (no Array.sort): scan the live spillable ranges of this
// class at (blockId, pos) and return the one with the LARGEST next-use
// distance. Tie-break deterministically by LARGER valueId so the choice is
// reproducible across builds. `calleeOnly` restricts to crossesCall ranges
// (callee-saved relief). Does NOT mutate `chosen` — caller commits.
//
// Scans `liveSet` (the O(pressure) range indices live at this position) rather
// than all ranges; every member is already live at (blockId, pos) by the
// sweep invariant, so no rangeLiveAt re-test is needed.
function selectFarthest(ranges LiveRangeArray, liveSet RegIntArray, regClass RegClass, blockId BlockId, pos RegInt, calleeOnly bool, blockArgPlumbing BoolArray, nextUse NextUseMap, chosen BoolArray, blockMaxPos RegIntArray, rpo RpoInfo, cfg CfgInfo) returns PickResult
	var bestDist = i64.min
	var bestVid = -1
	var best = LiveRange.create(-1)
	var found = false

	for idx in liveSet 'each'
		let range = try ranges.get(idx) otherwise panic("invariant: liveSet idx {idx} OOB in ranges")
		if not isSpillCandidate(range, regClass: regClass, blockArgPlumbing: blockArgPlumbing, chosen: chosen) 'notCandidate'
			continue
		end 'notCandidate'
		if calleeOnly and not range.crossesCall 'notCross'
			continue
		end 'notCross'

		let dist = nextUseFromPoint(range, blockId: blockId, fromPos: pos, rpo: rpo, nextUse: nextUse, blockMaxPos: blockMaxPos, cfg: cfg)
		let better = dist > bestDist or (dist == bestDist and range.valueId > bestVid)
		if not found or better 'takeIt'
			bestDist = dist
			bestVid = range.valueId
			best = range
			found = true
		end 'takeIt'
	end 'each'

	return PickResult.create(found, range: best)
end 'selectFarthest'

// Mark `range` chosen and push it into the decision's spilledRanges. Pushes
// the actual LiveRange object (as the reactive loop does) so allocateSpillSlots
// can partition by class and assign slots.
function commitSpill(decision SpillDecision, range LiveRange, chosen BoolArray)
	try chosen.set(range.valueId, value: true) otherwise panic("invariant: commitSpill chosen.set OOB; sized to maxVid+1")
	decision.spilledRanges.push(range)
	logTrace(LogCategory.ir, message: function() gives "belady: spill v={range.valueId} class={range.regClass.name} weight={range.spillWeight} crossesCall={range.crossesCall}")
end 'commitSpill'

// Mark `range` chosen and queue it for SPLITTING around its crossing call
// (see relievePressureAt phase (a)). Unlike commitSpill this does NOT add the
// range to spilledRanges, so Belady creates no reload for it — the reactive
// spill loop performs the call-boundary split later (its trySplitAtCall ends
// the value's interval before the call so it no longer consumes a callee-saved
// register across it). Marking chosen here keeps the sweep's demand tracker
// consistent with the post-split state. splitRanges is consumed only for the
// hand-off diagnostic in runBeladyPressureReduction.
function commitSplit(decision SpillDecision, range LiveRange, chosen BoolArray)
	try chosen.set(range.valueId, value: true) otherwise panic("invariant: commitSplit chosen.set OOB; sized to maxVid+1")
	decision.splitRanges.push(range)
	logTrace(LogCategory.ir, message: function() gives "belady: split-at-call v={range.valueId} class={range.regClass.name} weight={range.spillWeight} crossesCall={range.crossesCall}")
end 'commitSplit'
